WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>hoshi ga furishikiru penthouse de
In the penthouse that watches the stars fall...</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>sora no ORUGO-RU hitori kiiteta
I listened to Heaven's music box...</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.460
<i>GARASU no RO-PU wo mekakushi de wataru
Walking, blindfolded, across a tight-rope of glass...</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.090
<i>minna sabishii SA-KASU no kodomo sa
Everyone is like, the lonely child of the circus.</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>hitori bocchi no kanashimi ni
The rope that creaks with the sadness of isolation...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.770
<i>kishinda tsuna ga kokoro de yureteru...
...is still locked deep in my heart...</i>

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>yasashii me wo shita dareka ni aitai
I wish to meet the one who's eyes glow with warmth!</i>

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>sasayaite kureyo soba ni iruyotte Silent Voice
Whisper to me that you'll always be there by my side, Silent Voice.</i>

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:38.060
NAHEL ARGAMA

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.530
Seeing the colony
drop was a success,

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.250
Haman hurried to
seize control of space.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.290
Once we got wind of this,

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.850
we also headed for space
from a Karaba base in Norway.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.310
Internal cabin pressurization check.
IMU calibration complete.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.270
Coordinates are: north 28 degrees,
36 minutes, 30.32 seconds.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.860
Fare thee well, Argama.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.450
It was a good ship,
wasn't it? It's a shame.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.370
This doesn't mean it's gone.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.870
Karaba will be using it.
It's not going to waste.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.920
- One minute to launch!
- Beginning countdown!

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.460
Hang on tight, everyone!

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.500
Even in the latest models,
the g-forces can be pretty intense!

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.050
Says the one who's safe
in a cozy cockpit.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.470
Quit complaining. If we
go down, we all go together.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.800
Don't even joke about that!

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.050
It's hard to believe
we've made it this far.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.060
It's thanks to Haman's forces
having returned to space.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.850
Not like we can beat up every one of
the Earth Federation's higher-ups, huh?

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:04.110
Right. We couldn't save anyone,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.860
and now we're going to
board another spaceship.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.370
Judau...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.950
Nothing's over yet.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.160
It's because those guys on Earth
gave Haman Side 3.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.160
But can we finish it
by doing this?

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.080
That's why we
have to keep fighting.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.370
Okay then, let's do that!

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.680
Elle! What are you doing?!

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.180
I have my personal freedom!

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.580
GLASGOW

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.040
DAKAR

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.240
We're about to enter
the Side 4 shoal zone.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.370
Captain, where's
the La Vie en Rose?

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.760
There it is.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.550
What's that ship? It looks
just like the Argama, doesn't it?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.060
A new battleship,
the Nahel Argama.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.370
Nahel Argama?
Was it built at Granada?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.650
That's going to be
our new ship.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.780
Wow... the Nahel Argama.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.790
Emary Ounce.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.380
My thanks for your efforts, Captain Bright,
and to all of the Argama's crew.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.680
Thank you, Deputy Captain.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.250
Yes, sir.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.750
Welcome back, Mr. Judau!

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.220
Thanks.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.720
I'm amazed you're here.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.440
Great... him again?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:49.060
Captain Bright, now that you've
arrived, I'd like a word with you.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:49.790
Yes, sir.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.610
Captain, shouldn't we
inspect the Nahel Argama first?

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.400
Yes, there's that.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.070
Hey!

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:59.360
Milly, why don't you show Judau and
the others around the Nahel Argama?

00:05:59.360 --> 00:05:59.870
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.000
- Captain!
- Let's go!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.660
Nahel Argama means
"close to the Argama."

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.670
Close to the Argama?

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.550
Because it's inherited the
design concepts of the Argama.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.880
Awesome! It's nothing
but the latest hardware!

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.510
We could sell this for a fortune!

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.940
Mondo! Can't you ever stop
thinking like a junk dealer?

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.330
Still, I'd take this ship
as my severance package.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.980
Severance package?

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:32.650
Once we go to Side 3 and beat
Haman, the war will end, right?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.250
When that happens,
we'll be out of a job!

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.440
We can run a shipping company
using this thing.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.160
Nahel Argama Shipping, huh?

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:43.450
What do you think?
Looks simple to use, doesn't it?

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.280
Yeah.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.110
This should be the control system
for the main cannon.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.170
The high mega particle cannon
is a threefold system...

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:53.170
so you can use it via the gun platforms
or from the sub-bridge as well.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.470
Nice!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.860
All hands to level 1 battle stations!

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.430
Gunners, that barrage is too light!
What are you doing?!

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.050
Idiot.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.180
Who do you think you are?

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.180
Amateur.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.360
Really!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.160
So, this is the
mega particle cannon?

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:18.860
Activating catapult deck
guidance lights!

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.500
- Elle, you can do that?
- Leave it to me!

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.330
Hey!

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.920
- What are you doing?!
- Let go!

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.810
What are you doing?!

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.250
Checking the equipment!

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.540
Who gave you permission?!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.550
Do we need permission
to look around our own ship?!

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.930
"Our ship"?

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.260
They haven't told you
anything yet, have they?

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.760
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.110
We don't have to explain
that to a bunch of kids!

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.600
Who are you calling kids?!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.230
Judau, don't!

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:54.240
Deputy Captain Emary
authorized their entry here.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.520
No one told me, but...
fine. Now get out of here!

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.700
What was that?!

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.950
- Why, you...!
- l said don't!

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:06.080
Let's go to the mobile
suit deck, everyone.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.660
Is this how the AEUG treats us?!

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.550
You may call them Newtypes,
but in the end they're just children.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:26.180
And they willfully disregard our orders.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.810
So that's why you're kicking Judau
and the others off the Nahel Argama?!

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:33.060
While you were fighting
Neo Zeon on Earth,

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.020
we had time to
rebuild our organization.

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:38.540
We don't need to depend
on children anymore!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.070
Even after they've saved
us so many times?!

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.740
That won't work anymore.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.360
Haman seems to have
settled down at Side 3.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.990
All the more reason
we need their strength!

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.950
Adults should take over from now on.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.250
We're hurrying to organize a crew
and proceeding with pilot training.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.420
You're saying you don't need
the Argama's crew anymore?!

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.050
You're the sole exception,
Captain Bright.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.880
You will take command
of the Nahel Argama.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.130
I will not accept
this arbitrary decision!

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.470
You're in no position to choose.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.020
The choice belongs to
the AEUG's general staff!

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.730
Can you hear?

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:16.350
You shouldn't eavesdrop.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.320
Quiet!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.400
Would you get out of my way?!
Hey! Madchar!

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.820
Mr. Madchar, at least!

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:31.240
You're no different from
the Earth Federation bigwigs!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.950
Are you okay with
that load of crap, Captain?!

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.460
Hardly.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.920
No way! The captain had
to hurry back into space...

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:42.170
without getting to see
his wife and kids on Earth!

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:43.510
That's right.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.220
As it turns out, I should have
visited them instead!

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:51.470
Um, that is to say...

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.060
Like you kids know anything
about military organization?!

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:57.190
We've been doing great
in actual combat!

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.480
The reason the Argama's
had such a tough time...

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.460
was because the AEUG's general staff
wasn't serious about crushing Haman!

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.360
What do you mean
the AEUG wasn't serious?!

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.160
That's why you gave
Side 3 to Haman!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:11.620
I-It was the Earth Federation
that made that decision.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.720
Meaning the AEUG
couldn't stop them!

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.750
The guys on Earth and the moon
don't know how tough the colonies have it!

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:19.960
Why, you...!

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:22.040
Commander, please calm down!

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.900
C-Captain Bright!

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.980
It's your poor training that's
made them like this!

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:30.050
I never could teach
them any manners.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:31.640
I don't like it, either.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.100
Captain!

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.110
An enemy attack?!

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.750
Illia Pazom.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.250
Yes, sir.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.510
Take this.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.340
Master Mashymre...

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:12.840
I dropped a colony and
stole the lives of many people.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.720
This rose weighs heavily upon me.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.490
You're a romantic,
aren't you, Master Mashymre?

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:20.350
A knight should also be a poet.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:23.270
Ferocity alone makes one
no better than an animal.

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:25.940
Shangri-La was full
of people like that.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:28.990
Master Mashymre,
our recon team has returned.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:35.470
They say our enemy consists of a
dock ship and an Argama-class cruiser.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:38.870
Argama-class?
Could it be a new ship?

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:43.330
Recall the recon team!
Go to level 1 battle stations!

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.540
Prepare to launch all Zssa units!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.090
Suppression fire into enemy airspace!

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.760
One volley every 10 seconds!

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.470
Charge laterally into their airspace
without decelerating!

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.770
Route the Zssa team
around our line of fire!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.190
Turn bow 15 degrees to port!
Open fire!

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.660
You guys aren't qualified to sortie!

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:22.370
If we don't, the La Vie en Rose
and the Nahel Argama will be destroyed!

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.670
I'm still a soldier!
When a superior issues orders...!

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:27.590
Fortunately, I'm not a soldier!

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.890
What the hell are you doing?!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.510
If we don't do something,
the Nahel Argama...

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.260
and the La Vie en Rose
will be destroyed!

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:37.550
Why, you little...
don't be so arrogant!

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.350
Just because you have
a little mobile suit piloting skill!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:40.970
Stop that!

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:42.730
He's just a kid!

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:44.060
What are you doing?!

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.770
They're getting in the way!

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:47.900
What's the point of
fighting your allies?!

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.440
These children are
disobeying orders!

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.860
This is no time to
be talking like that!

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.280
That was a direct hit!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:00.170
You go, too!
Don't let those kids beat you!

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.790
Sir!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.970
He's already beat.
Completely.

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:18.550
You!

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.390
- Energy, go!
- Cameras, activated!

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:21.720
- Searching for enemies!
- All gun turrets!

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:23.180
Starboard!

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.560
You guys can handle it!

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.770
But, Captain...!

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.270
You two, man the turrets!

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.560
Why?!

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.860
Do you always question
your orders?! Get going!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:31.860
A-Aye, sir!

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:33.570
Way to go!

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.570
Release docking arms!

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.280
Captain.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.820
- Right! Man your stations!
- Aye, sir!

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.990
Nahel Argama,
hurry up and launch!

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:42.790
Get those kids off this ship!

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.950
Forget it! There's no time!

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.080
Release the Nahel Argama!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.880
At this rate,
we'll both be destroyed!

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.380
Deputy Captain!

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:53.590
Prepare to launch!

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:55.260
All arms, disengaged!

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.550
Right! Nahel Argama...

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:59.470
Captain Bright!
Let me say the next part.

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:01.520
Nahel Argama, launch!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.650
All units have fired their missiles!

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:13.320
Okay, fall back!
Leave it for the next wave!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.990
Enemies, withdrawing!

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:21.040
Right! That means the next
group's coming! Look sharp!

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:24.330
Beecha, I'm giving
you command for now.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.290
Huh?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.870
If you're up for this,
you need to get used to it.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.670
I'm going to inspect the ship.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.880
All right then,
I'm in command!

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.300
- Look, I wouldn't say no, but...
- Don't take it seriously!

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.960
You get what you're told to do, right?

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.890
- This isn't a game!
- Oh, boy...

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.550
- I said move!
- No!

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.550
You kids, stand aside!

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:44.970
What are you doing?!
Shinta! Qum!

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:45.680
Mr. Bright!

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:49.060
They wouldn't follow orders
and left the turrets!

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:52.980
We're bridge crew, not gunners!
Why would you use us like this?!

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.920
Is it because we're new here?!

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.420
Right now, it's better to have
people with combat experience!

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.900
But...!

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:01.280
Single mobile suit, to starboard!

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:03.870
Wh-Why is there just one?
Captain!

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.370
He left this to you!

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.080
- But...!
- I'm going out!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.750
Uh, right! GO!

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:14.470
A brand-new warship, eh?
Fine prey for me!

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:23.850
Shinta! Qum!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.650
Shinta! Qum!

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:42.250
- Judau Ashta! Double Zeta, here I go!
- Go!

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:50.380
Never seen that
mobile suit before.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.380
Is that a Gundam?
l don't believe it.

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.470
It's fast! Where's...?

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.110
What are you looking at?!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.610
What?!

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.060
Wh-What was...?

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.270
Why did that just happen?

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:19.150
There's no barrage at all!
Gunners!

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.650
No one's manning the guns!

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:21.650
What?!

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:23.150
The captain's gone out!

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:23.950
Huh?!

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.570
Transfer gunnery control to bridge!

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.370
The captain's in that launch!

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.080
That's insane!
He'll be shot down!

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:33.250
I'll cover him with the Mk. II!

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.180
Elle! Don't go out
of your own accord! Hey!

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.180
Huh? A launch
from the Nahel Argama?

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:44.180
Why are you being so careless?!

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:46.390
Again!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.560
What kind of trick was that, Double Zeta?

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.360
It was like electricity
running through my body.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.360
All Zssa units
are returning, sir!

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.730
What? Why are
they coming back?!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.780
This battle isn't over yet!

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.360
They apparently exhausted
their missiles, sir.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.570
They what?!

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:09.500
Bring them all up to the bridge!
I'll teach them a lesson!

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.960
Hang on! I'll save you!

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.890
A cable! Grab it!

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.180
What are you doing?!

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.560
Rescuing my crew comes first!

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:32.060
Captain Bright?!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.470
They're my crew, for now.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:34.770
Then I'll use the Double Zeta!

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:37.190
It's okay! Once they're recovered,
I'll head for the La Vie en Rose.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:38.770
You watch for the enemy!

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:40.360
R-Right...

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:45.870
You bastard!
Don't shoot missiles here!

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.500
It's fast!

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.250
I won't lose to anyone!

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.880
Wh-What power...!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:07.430
It's running?!

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.260
If I try fighting at its pace,
I'll exhaust myself.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.230
How do I play this...?
Of course!

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.420
Is he ever coming out?

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:28.370
Why does that
pilot irritate me so?

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:46.130
Where are you, Double Zeta?

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:47.600
There!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.940
What? Does he think
so little of me? Or else...

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:59.190
You have no plan!
You're just a fool, Gundam!

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.070
What are you aiming at?

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.830
I have you!
What?!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.870
What are you doing?!

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.170
I'm doing THIS!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.510
You seriously fight like that?!
Don't make a fool of me!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.460
I'm dead serious!

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:32.550
What can you do in a normal suit?

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:34.760
Things don't always go
like in your textbooks!

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:35.550
I'll crush you!

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:36.770
Just try!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.650
So easy to bait!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.910
Again?!

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.740
I'll never forgive you!

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.380
If I weren't damaged, I'd...!

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.750
Judau, where's Captain Bright?

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:07.680
He headed for the La Vie en Rose!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.930
Judau, what happened?

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.060
Why do you think
you have beam sabers?

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:24.270
Don't any of you have the
stomach for fighting Gundams?!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:26.150
Master Mashymre,
we understand, but...

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:29.070
Shut your mouth!
You have no right to speak!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.450
Illia, you've returned.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.880
The rose...

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.170
I beg your pardon, sir.

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:47.180
It was destroyed by
the Double Zeta's pilot.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:51.710
The rose...
Lady Haman's rose...!

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:55.180
Double Zeta! Judau Ashta!

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:56.970
That pilot...!

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:00.640
I see. So, that was Judau Ashta.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.480
Judau! Good job!

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:10.650
What about the enemy ship?

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.860
Still out there.

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:13.860
Let's get away from
the La Vie en Rose.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:15.650
We're the enemy's target.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:18.160
If we stay together, the La Vie
en Rose will get caught up in this.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.370
What about Captain Bright?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.290
Let him get some rest on
the La Vie en Rose.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.580
He's not so young, is he?

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:27.080
Yeah, thanks to all the
stress you guys give him.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.250
He's getting more
and more gray hairs!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.670
We'll head for the moon
for the time being.

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:32.880
Right, Beecha?

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:33.920
Exactly!

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.260
And ultimately, we'll push into Side 3.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.470
For a one-on-one
fight with Haman!

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.180
Let's go, Deputy Captain!

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:42.260
Right! All hands,
to your stations!

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:43.180
We ARE!

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:45.180
Nahel Argama, launch!

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:46.650
Yeah!

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:55.860
Farewell, again.

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:59.370
Send an optical signal.
"Good hunting, Nahel Argama."

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:02.280
How about "Farewell, Captain Bright"?

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:04.290
We can't say that.

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.520
Captain Bright!

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:12.460
But what about the Nahel Argama?

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.760
Mr. Torres and the others
are aboard, aren't they?

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:18.520
B-But how can a ship
move without its captain?

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:21.480
I wouldn't know.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:27.390
Good luck, everyone.

00:22:27.390 --> 00:22:31.490
Try as hard as
your own strengths will allow!

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:50.820
<i>ikuyaku ikuman ikuoku no hoshi yo
Hundreds upon thousands upon millions of stars...</i>

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:56.950
<i>naze hikaru dake nano ka kataru chikara no shiwase
...why do you just sit there and twinkle? Show me the power that lets me connect!</i>

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>Ima nara ore demo furikaerasu ni tobitatsu kokoro
For now, even I've got a mind that wanders without reminiscing past regrets!</i>

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Hoshi no kazu dake inochi wo takuwareba
If lives are really stored in the form of stars...</i>

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.940
<i>ginga no mure no hikari wo kaete misero
...show me how to change the light and move galaxies...</i>

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:29.650
<i>kono te ga tsukamu inochi no omosa ni naru
The weight of life itself, will be held in my hands!</i>

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>mada meinai yo sora no michishirude wa
Space's guidepost is still not within my sights...</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:41.620
<i>kono te ni saware hikari isenmanen
Let the light of 10 million years touch this hand!</i>

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:49.300
The La Vie en Rose
delivered some supplies to us,

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:52.220
but Emary's heart still
yearns for Bright.

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:56.550
Just then, the ship's attacked
by three mobile armors.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.170
Are all mobile armors
this amazing?

00:23:59.170 --> 00:24:01.720
As I deal with Beecha's
loss of faith in me.

00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:04.560
I wonder if we're
ready to face Side 3!

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:09.230
Next time, on Gundam ZZ:
"The Iron Wall of Jamru Fin."

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.930
Next Time

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.930
THE IRON WALL OF JAMRU FIN

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:10.810
Leina!
